CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ derived-to-base pack-parameter call in a function body: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/4.3: a function parameter that is a class template-id
(`Base<_Head, _Tail...>&`) is deduced from the base class of a derived-class
argument (`Derived<int>` -> `Base<int>`, so `_Head = int`, `_Tail` empty).

Regression: instantiating the callee with an empty trailing pack `_Tail` used
to drop the whole parameter `__b` -- its type `Base<_Head, _Tail...>&`
references the empty pack `_Tail` nested in a template-argument expansion -- so
`get_head<int>` was left with an empty parameter list and an unbindable call
(returning a nondet value).  Per N5008 [temp.variadic]/7 the empty expansion
only collapses the argument list (`Base<_Head>`); the parameter must be kept.
Fixed by restricting the empty-pack parameter removal in
cpp_instantiate_template.cpp to genuine function parameter packs (a top-level
`...`), not parameters that merely reference the pack nested in a template-id.
Assertion 2 (a wrong value) FAILs, proving non-vacuity.
